#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan D7, THE NEGATIVE HALF: the static guarantees a Saffron
;; file KEEPS.
;;
;; D7's first draft listed five feature families as unavailable in Saffron --
;; regions, GADTs, sessions, linearity/uniqueness, and borrows -- on the
;; premise that "an `any` cannot carry these guarantees".  Measured, that
;; premise holds for exactly ONE of them.
;;
;; Only `with-region` is genuinely downgraded, because its proof reads the
;; INFERRED RESULT TYPE of the bracket body, which is the one thing Saffron
;; makes `any` (see tests/fixtures/errors/saffron-region-bracket-refused).
;;
;; The other four are proved from things `any` never touches:
;;
;;   defgadt    constructor return types are ANNOTATIONS, and D2 keeps
;;              annotations legal in Saffron -- skolem escape still fires.
;;   Session P  the protocol lives in the annotation -- TUR-E0211 still
;;              fires, with the same protocol state.
;;   ^linear    a use-count walk over the body -- TUR-E0101 still fires.
;;   &T &mut T  a scope walk over uses -- the aliasing conflict still fires.
;;
;; This fixture is the guard against a later reading of the plan's original
;; list taking them away.  It is a POSITIVE fixture on purpose: it compiles
;; and runs, so it asserts the features are usable, not merely that some
;; diagnostic fires.  The matching negative assertions -- that each checker
;; still REJECTS a violation in a Saffron file -- live in
;; tests/fixtures/errors/saffron-linear-used-twice and its siblings.
;;
;; `area` annotates its scrutinee `: Shape` rather than leaving it `any`, and
;; that is a WORKAROUND, not a preference: matching an UNANNOTATED (`any`)
;; scrutinee against a PARAMETRIC ADT emits uncompilable C ("aggregate value
;; used where an integer was expected" -- the tagged aggregate is cast to a
;; pointer).  Filed as
;; docs/reported/saffron-match-any-scrutinee-on-parametric-adt-emits-bad-c.md.
;;
;; That report was first written as a `defgadt` bug and it is not one: a
;; parametric `defdata` fails identically and a non-parametric one works, so
;; the axis is ARITY, not `defgadt`.  The annotation here keeps THIS fixture
;; about D7 rather than about that bug.
(defdata Shape [a]
  (Sq  int : (Shape int))
  (Rec int int : (Shape int)))

(defn area [s : Shape]
  (match s
    (Sq  w)   (* w w)
    (Rec w h) (* w h)))

(defn borrowed []
  (let [x 21]
    (let [r (& x)]
      (* @r 2))))

(defn main []
  (println (cast (area (Sq 6)) int))
  (println (cast (area (Rec 3 4)) int))
  (println (cast (borrowed) int))
  0)
